# Project Conventions

Living reference for small, cross-cutting rules. Add new items here as patterns emerge.

## File Names

- Use **kebab-case** for all file and directory names.

```text
# ❌ BAD
UserProfile.tsx
staff.ts

# ✅ GOOD
user-profile.tsx
staff.ts
```

## Database & Domain Naming

- Use **singular** names for tables, entities, modules, and domain folders — not plural.

```text
# ❌ BAD
users
clinics
staff_members

# ✅ GOOD
user
clinic
staff
```

Applies to: SQL/ORM table names, Drizzle models, TypeScript modules, API route segments, and ERD/DBML definitions.

## TypeScript & Modules

- Use **named exports** only — no default exports.
- When a function has more than two parameters, use a **single object parameter**.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
export default function createUser(name: string, email: string, role: string) {}

// ✅ GOOD
export function createUser(params: CreateUserParams) {
  const { name, email, role } = params;
}
```
